  "lineage": "Punjabi-language pop crystallised in the early 1990s across Jalandhar, Delhi and the UK diaspora as folk boliyan and tappe were set to programmed beats — Malkit Singh, Gurdas Maan and Daler Mehndi's cassette-era hits established the form of a driving 100-140 BPM dhol chaal with tumbi or algoza riff, harmonium or synth chord stabs, and an open-throated declamatory tenor with sharp gamak-like grace notes — remade after 2010 by Diljit Dosanjh and the Punjabi-Canadian axis into a slick DAW production still anchored to the dhol pattern.",
